   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volume_Two_%28The_Soft_Machine_album%29",
   "resumo_en": "Volume Two is the second album by the British band Soft Machine, released in September 1969, through Probe Records. It was Soft Machine's first album release in the UK. \nRecording sessions ran from February to March 1969 at Olympic Studios in London, produced by the band themselves. The album combined humour, dada, psychedelia, progressive rock, and jazz rock. Upon its release, the album peaked at number 2 on the Dutch Album Top 100, and was positively received by music critics. In 2000, it was voted number 715 in Colin Larkin's All Time Top 1000 Albums.",
